# Statement

The finite S3 twisted Chan-Paton cancellation is:

```text
not the smooth selected source theorem.
```

```text
S3 sees rank(F_3^2) = 2,
ordinary DD(B)|S3 = nonzero,
S3 carries the q79/F,m=1 projective qutrit Chan-Paton module,
the twisted CP class matches the pulled-back zeta_3^2 gerbe class.
```

Thus the ordinary S3 DD-zero route still fails, but the finite twisted-bundle
route cancels the obstruction in the finite quotient convention.

# Inputs

The proof uses:

```text
minimal equivariant stack selector = S3,
q79/F,m=1 finite gerbe class = zeta_3^2,
projective qutrit carrier validates with that same twist,
S1 and S2 remain rank <= 1 ordinary D7 stacks,
C12,C23,C31 remain ordinary DD-zero matter curves,
visible complex worldvolume W3/spinC gate is closed.
```

# What This Closes

It closes:

```text
finite rank-two S3 DD obstruction is cancellable by twisted CP,
S3 finite CP source class matches the q79/F,m=1 twist,
ordinary matter-curve DD-zero behavior is retained.
```

# What It Does Not Close

It does not close:

```text
selected smooth S3 Deligne/Cech source,
fixed differential-cohomology refinement of the finite class,
Green-Schwarz/Bianchi verification for the smooth source,
full Freed-Witten verification for the smooth source,
projector retention,
selected visible operator source,
selected D_E/dotD,
primitive C1 contractions,
full SM closure.
```

In particular, projector retention remains open.

# Conclusion

The blocker has moved again.  We no longer merely know that S3 is the selected
stack; we now know that its finite rank-two obstruction is the right kind of
obstruction for the qutrit twisted Chan-Paton module.  The next missing object
is the smooth selected S3 source theorem, not another finite S3 choice.
